flowchart TD
    Start["&lt;b&gt;Analyze Clause Intent&lt;/b&gt;"] --&gt; Q1{"Is it a direct directive&lt;br&gt;issued to the listener?"}
    Q1 -- "Yes" --&gt; Imperative["&lt;b&gt;IMPERATIVE MOOD&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Covert [you] subject&lt;br&gt;• Bare base verb: &lt;i&gt;'Halt!'&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Negation requires: &lt;i&gt;'Do not touch!'&lt;/i&gt;"]
    Q1 -- "No" --&gt; Q2{"Does it assert, inquire, or&lt;br&gt;assume an open fact in reality?"}
    Q2 -- "Yes" --&gt; Indicative["&lt;b&gt;INDICATIVE MOOD (Realis)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Factual assertions & inquiries&lt;br&gt;• Zero, First, & Open Past Conditionals&lt;br&gt;• Standard tense conjugation & do-support"]
    Q2 -- "No" --&gt; Q3{"Is it a command or mandate&lt;br&gt;in a subordinate that-clause?"}
    Q3 -- "Yes" --&gt; Mandative["&lt;b&gt;MANDATIVE SUBJUNCTIVE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Bare base verb in that-clause&lt;br&gt;• Invariant 'be'&lt;br&gt;• Direct negation: 'not' + base (no 'do')"]
    Q3 -- "No" --&gt; Q4{"Is it explicitly contrary&lt;br&gt;to present or past reality?"}
    Q4 -- "Yes" --&gt; Counterfactual["&lt;b&gt;COUNTERFACTUAL SUBJUNCTIVE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Invariant 'were' for all persons&lt;br&gt;• Inversion: &lt;i&gt;'Were he to resign...'&lt;/i&gt;"]
    Q4 -- "No" --&gt; Formulaic["&lt;b&gt;FORMULAIC SUBJUNCTIVE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Fossilized idioms&lt;br&gt;• &lt;i&gt;'Be that as it may'&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;'Suffice it to say'&lt;/i&gt;"]
